            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#West01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+West"}> Peter West
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 11
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{11}
                  and M theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0104081"} arXiv:hep-th/0104081
          %p
            A precursor to (
            %a{:href => "#West01"}> West 01
            ) is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernard+Julia"}> Bernard Julia
              ,
              %em Dualities in the classical supergravity limits
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9805083"}> arXiv:hep-th/9805083
              )
          %p
            as explained in (
            %a{:href => "#HenneauxJuliaLevie10"}> Henneaux-Julia-Levie 10
            ).
          %p
            The derivation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            and maximally supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5d+supergravity"} 5d supergravity
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            with values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product"} semidirect product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
